    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d553">

                <pb facs="0664" n="578" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg578"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Combs to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States,<lb/>Guatemala and
                                Honduras</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-03-18"><hi rendition="#italic">March 18,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 36.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to attach copy of a report
                    received from W. Heyden, United States consular agent at Amapala, for the
                    information of the Department.</p>
                <p>President Estrada informed me a few days since his information was that Bonilla
                    was making a successful struggle; that Bonilla’s forces were drawing closer and
                    closer to Tegucigalpa both from the east and from the west.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Leslie Combs.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d553-a1.xml" xpointer="d553-a1"/>
            </div>
